Jerusalem) i.e. between the two walls of the Ophel and the southwest hill respectively, of a reservoir Isa 22:11 , a gate 2Kin 25:4 = Jer 34:4 = 52:7 ; symbol of Israel, Amos 7:7 ; 2Chr 8:5 ; 14:6 ; 25:23 ; 26:6 (3 t. in verse); Psalm 51:20; Neh 1:3 31t. in Nehemiah; אֲנָךְ חוֺמַת Amos 7:7 (literally wall of a plummet ) is of doubtful meaning: a wall built plumb , or by means of a plumb-line ? We thinks unintelligible; חוֺמָה עִיר = walled city , Lev 25:29 , ח לֹא אשׁר ׳עִיר 25:30 ( לֹא = לוֺ ), opposed to ח להם אין אשׁר ׳הַחֲצֵרִים 25:31 (all H); more elaborately ח בְּצֻרֹת ׳עָרִים וּבְרִ֑יחַ דְּלָתַיִם גְבֹהָה Deut 3:5 , compare 2Chr 8:5 ; ׳ע נְחשֶׁת וּבְרִיחַ חוֺמָה גְּדֹלוֺת 1Kin 4:13 ; ח ׳בְצוּרָה Isa 2:15 ; ׳ח singular of wall of Jerusalem 1Kin 3:1 + often; contempt. אַבְנֵיהֶם חוֺמַת Nehemiah 3:35; less often plural Neh 2:13 +; of specific portions of wall ׳ח הָעֹפֶל 2Chr 27:3 ; Neh 3:27 ; ׳ח הַשֶּׁלַח בְּרֵבַת 3:15 ; הָֽרְחָבָה ׳הַח 3:8 ; 12:38 ; also (generally) of Babylon Jer 51:58 . &#8212; Men build , בנה , the ׳ח 1Kin 9:15 +, especially (of rebuilding), Neh 2:17 +; fortify it בִּצֵּר Isa 22:10 ; it is joined together קשׁר Nehemiah 3:38; is repaired לְח אֲרוּכָה ׳עָֽלְתָה Neh 4:1 ; it falls נפל Josh 6:5 , 20 ; 1Kin 20:30 ; Ezek 38:20 ; the enemy makes it fall הִמִּיל 2Sam 20:15 (preceded by מַשְׁחִית si vera lectio, see Dr); destroys it הִשְׁחִית Lam 2:8 ; שִׁהֵת Ezek 26:4 ; makes a breach in it בּ ׳מָּרַץ 2Kin 14:13 2Chr 25:23 , compare פרץ with accusative 26:6 ; Nehemiah 3:35, and הַמְּרוּצָה אֶתכֿלהֿח ׳וֶיִּבֶן 32:5 ; also (in simile) ח ואין מְּרוּצָה ׳עִיר Prov 25:28 ; and Punic participle מְפֹרָ֑צֶת Neh 1:3 ; one breakes it down נָתַץ 2Kin 25:10 ; 2Chr 36:19 ; Jer 39:8 ; 52:14 ; tears it down הָרַס Ezek 26:12 , compare passive Jer 50:15 ; Amos predicts that ׳י will send fire into wall (of Gaza, etc.): בְּח אֵשׁ ׳וְשִׁלַּחְתִּי Amos 1:7 , 10 ; or kindle fire in בְּח אֵשׁ ׳וְהִצַּתִּי vAmos 1:14, so Jer 49:27 . 2 wall of a building: a. citadel, fortress ; ׳ח ארמנותיה Lam 2:7 . b. surrounding new temple Ezek 40:5 ; 42:20 . 3 figurative of waters of Red Sea Exod 14:22 , 29 (P), compare Nahum 3:8 ; of David's men as protectors of Nabal's shepherds 1Sam 25:16 ; of prophet as object of assault נְחשֶׁת חוֺמַת Jer 1:18 ; ׳ח בְּצוּרָה נחשׁת 15:20 ; of strong, virtuous woman Song 8:9-10 , of salvation, יְשׁוּעָה , as defence Isa 26:1 (|| חֵל ); of ׳י himself אֵשׁ ׳ח Zech 2:9 ; a dangerous political scheme is called breach in ׳ח נִשְׁגָּבָה Isa 30:13 ; ׳ח נִשְׂגָּבָה in simile of wealth Prov 18:11 (|| עֻזּוֺ קִרְיַת ); a reckless man is ח אֵין מְּרוּצָה ׳עִיר 25:28 .","rootNote":"feminine active participle of an unused root apparently meaning to join ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Kgs 3 1","keyReferences":["1Kgs 3 1","1Kgs 4 13","1Kgs 9 15","1Kgs 20 30","1Sam 25 16","1Sam 31 10","1Sam 31 12","2Chr 8 5"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":133,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Kgs 3 1","book":"1Kgs","chapter":3,"verse":1,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"חוֹמַ֥ת","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcfsc"},{"reference":"1Kgs 4 13","book":"1Kgs","chapter":4,"verse":13,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"חוֹמָ֖ה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcfsa"},{"reference":"1Kgs 9 15","book":"1Kgs","chapter":9,"verse":15,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"חוֹמַ֣ת","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcfsc"},{"reference":"1Kgs 20 30","book":"1Kgs","chapter":20,"verse":30,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הַ/חוֹמָ֔ה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ncfsa"},{"reference":"1Sam 25 16","book":"1Sam","chapter":25,"verse":16,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"חוֹמָה֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcfsa"},{"reference":"1Sam 31 10","book":"1Sam","chapter":31,"verse":10,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"בְּ/חוֹמַ֖ת","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Ncfsc"},{"reference":"1Sam 31 12","book":"1Sam","chapter":31,"verse":12,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"מֵ/חוֹמַ֖ת","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Ncf